<div id="p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:144%;">Supplementary Material 
<br class="ltx_break"></span></p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix ltx_align_left">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>The detailed derivation of SAG-ODE</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides the formal derivation for the SAG-ODE introduced in the main paper. We restate the governing equation for a given stage <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, which operates on the active token set <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}(t)}{\mathrm{d}t}=\mathbf{\Pi}_{k}\,\bm{u}_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathbf{y}(t),t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}(t)}{\mathrm{d}t}=\mathbf{\Pi}_{k}\,\bm{u}_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathbf{y}(t),t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the augmented lifter operator, and the term <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{S}_{k}^{\top}\mathbf{y}(t),t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{S}_{k}^{\top}\mathbf{y}(t),t)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the velocity computed by the Transformer using only the <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> active tokens. The following derivation shows how this compact form is obtained by starting from an exact orthogonal decomposition of the ideal velocity field and then applying the proposed approximation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Derivation via orthogonal decomposition</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}^{*}(\mathbf{y},t)=\bm{u}_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{y},t)\in\mathbb{R}^{Nd}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}^{*}(\mathbf{y},t)=\bm{u}_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{y},t)\in\mathbb{R}^{Nd}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the ideal, full-dimensional velocity field that acts on all <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> tokens. Using the projection matrix <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{k}=\mathbf{S}_{k}\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{k}=\mathbf{S}_{k}\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can decompose this velocity field into two orthogonal components: One lying within the subspace spanned by the anchor tokens (active subspace) and the other in its orthogonal complement (inactive subspace). The decomposition is given by</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}^{*}=\mathbf{P}_{k}\bm{v}^{*}+(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{P}_{k})\bm{v}^{*}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}^{*}=\mathbf{P}_{k}\bm{v}^{*}+(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{P}_{k})\bm{v}^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{k}=\mathbf{S}_{k}\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{k}=\mathbf{S}_{k}\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> into the first term, we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}^{*}=\mathbf{S}_{k}(\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\bm{v}^{*})+(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{P}_{k})\bm{v}^{*}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}^{*}=\mathbf{S}_{k}(\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\bm{v}^{*})+(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{P}_{k})\bm{v}^{*},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\bm{v}^{*}\in\mathbb{R}^{m_{k}d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\bm{v}^{*}\in\mathbb{R}^{m_{k}d}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the precise velocity projected onto the <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> anchor tokens.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Approximation strategy</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Computing the full velocity <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is computationally prohibitive. To accelerate inference, we introduce two coherent approximations corresponding to the two terms in the decomposition:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sparse input approximation (active component):</span> Instead of computing the velocity based on the full context <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, we approximate the active component by evaluating the network only on the projected anchor tokens <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{R}^{m_{k}d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{R}^{m_{k}d}</annotation></semantics></math>. We define this computable sparse velocity as</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{u}}:=\bm{u}_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathbf{y},t)\in\mathbb{R}^{m_{k}d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{u}}:=\bm{u}_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathbf{y},t)\in\mathbb{R}^{m_{k}d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the first term in Eq. (<a href="#A1.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ A.1 Derivation via orthogonal decomposition ‣ Appendix A The detailed derivation of SAG-ODE ‣ Just-in-Time: Training-Free Spatial Acceleration for Diffusion Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) is approximated by the embedding of this sparse calculation <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}_{k}\tilde{\bm{u}}\in\mathbb{R}^{Nd}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}_{k}\tilde{\bm{u}}\in\mathbb{R}^{Nd}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Subspace extrapolation (inactive component):</span> For the second term <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{P}_{k})\bm{v}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{P}_{k})\bm{v}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, which represents the velocity of the inactive tokens, we avoid explicit neural function evaluations. Instead, we assume that the dynamics of the inactive tokens can be reasonably inferred from the active anchors via a pre-defined interpolation operator <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> (please refer to Appendix <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Implementation of interpolation operators ‣ Appendix B Implementation details ‣ Just-in-Time: Training-Free Spatial Acceleration for Diffusion Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> for specific implementation details). This yields the approximation</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{P}_{k})\bm{v}^{*}\approx\mathcal{I}_{k}(\tilde{\bm{u}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{P}_{k})\bm{v}^{*}\approx\mathcal{I}_{k}(\tilde{\bm{u}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Synthesis and the augmented lifter</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting the approximations from the previous section, the approximate velocity field <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is formed by combining the exact velocity for the anchor tokens with the interpolated velocity for the inactive ones. We now define the augmented lifter <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> as the operator that encapsulates this entire process. Its action on the computed sparse velocity <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{u}}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}=\mathbf{\Pi}_{k}\tilde{\bm{u}}:=\mathbf{S}_{k}\tilde{\bm{u}}+\mathcal{I}_{k}(\tilde{\bm{u}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}=\mathbf{\Pi}_{k}\tilde{\bm{u}}:=\mathbf{S}_{k}\tilde{\bm{u}}+\mathcal{I}_{k}(\tilde{\bm{u}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This definition states that the operator <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> maps the sparse velocity to the full space. By substituting <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{u}}=\bm{u}_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathbf{y},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{u}}=\bm{u}_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathbf{y},t)</annotation></semantics></math>, we arrive at the final, compact form of our SAG-ODE:</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}(t)}{\mathrm{d}t}=\mathbf{\Pi}_{k}\bm{u}_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathbf{y}(t),t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}(t)}{\mathrm{d}t}=\mathbf{\Pi}_{k}\bm{u}_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathbf{y}(t),t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Proof of consistency</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Applying the projection <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> to the derived ODE confirms that the dynamics on the activate anchor tokens remain exact relative to the sparse computation:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}}{\mathrm{d}t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}}{\mathrm{d}t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}(\mathbf{S}_{k}\tilde{\bm{u}}+\mathcal{I}_{k}(\tilde{\bm{u}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}(\mathbf{S}_{k}\tilde{\bm{u}}+\mathcal{I}_{k}(\tilde{\bm{u}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathbf{S}_{k})\tilde{\bm{u}}+\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathcal{I}_{k}(\tilde{\bm{u}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathbf{S}_{k})\tilde{\bm{u}}+\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathcal{I}_{k}(\tilde{\bm{u}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{I}\cdot\tilde{\bm{u}}+\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{I}\cdot\tilde{\bm{u}}+\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{u}_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathbf{y},t)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{u}_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathbf{y},t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we utilize the property that <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathbf{S}_{k}=\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathbf{S}_{k}=\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math> (orthonormality of the selector) and <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathcal{I}_{k}(\cdot)=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}^{\top}_{k}\mathcal{I}_{k}(\cdot)=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (the interpolation operator has no effect on the anchor subspace by design). This concludes the derivation.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix ltx_align_left">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Implementation details</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide further implementation details of our JiT framework, including the specific construction of the selector matrix <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for the initial stage, the algorithm for our interpolation operators <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the detailed hyperparameter configurations for the experimental results reported in the main text.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.10744v1/check.png" id="A2.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:411/195;" width="411" height="195" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="A2.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">An illustration of the construction process for the initial selector matrix <math id="A2.F5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. </span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Construction of the initial selector matrix</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As described in Sec. <a href="#S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" title="Importance-guided token activation ‣ 3.3 Deterministic micro-flow ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Just-in-Time: Training-Free Spatial Acceleration for Diffusion Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, for all subsequent stages <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;K</annotation></semantics></math>, anchor tokens are selected dynamically based on the importance map derived from the velocity field variance. Consequently, we only need to define the construction of the selector matrix <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> for the initial and most sparse stage.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For this initialization, our primary objective is to capture the global semantic structure while strictly adhering to the sparsity budget. To achieve this, we employ a deterministic strided grid initialization strategy, reinforced by explicit boundary constraints. Specifically, this strategy subsamples the latent grid with a fixed stride of 2 in both the height and width dimensions, which is akin to selecting the top-left token from every non-overlapping <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 2</annotation></semantics></math> block. To ensure the integrity of the image frame and prevent boundary artifacts, we augment this set by explicitly including all tokens located at the top, bottom, left, and right boundaries of the latent feature map.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since the number of tokens resulting from this geometric pattern may not strictly align with the target budget <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, we apply a final stochastic adjustment step. If the number of geometrically selected tokens falls short of <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, we randomly sample supplementary indices from the remaining inactive set to fill the deficit. Conversely, if the count exceeds <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, we randomly drop excess tokens from the generated set to strictly meet the <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> budget. This hybrid approach combines the regularity required for low-frequency structure generation with the flexibility to meet precise computational constraints. We provide a simplified schematic diagram of the above process in <a href="#A2.F5" title="In Appendix B Implementation details ‣ Just-in-Time: Training-Free Spatial Acceleration for Diffusion Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Implementation of interpolation operators</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It should be clarified that while sharing the same algorithmic implementation, the two interpolation operators serve distinct roles within our framework, the subspace extrapolation operator <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> acts on the velocity field <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas the structural prior operator <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> operates on the data latent tokens <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We opt for a combination of nearest-neighbor interpolation and masked Gaussian blur rather than standard linear (e.g., bilinear) interpolation. This choice is driven by the nature of the high-dimensional representations in DiTs. Velocity fields and latent states often exhibit high-frequency spatial variations and complex semantic structures. Linear-based interpolation assumes a smooth gradient between sparse anchors, which can lead to over-smoothed features that drift off the valid feature manifold, particularly when the spatial grid is irregular or highly sparse.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In contrast, nearest-neighbor interpolation strictly preserves the original feature statistics and signal integrity of the anchor tokens. We then address the resulting spatial discontinuities (blockiness) via a controlled Gaussian blur, which smooths the transition boundaries without corrupting the feature values at the anchor positions. Specifically, derived from the token sparsity <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, we approximate the average anchor gap as <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L\approx\rho^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≈</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\approx\rho^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>. We dynamically set the blur scale <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.4L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.4L</annotation></semantics></math> such that the effective radius of the Gaussian kernel (<math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\sigma\approx 1.2L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1.2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\sigma\approx 1.2L</annotation></semantics></math>) slightly exceeds and covers this gap. This geometric constraint systematically suppresses blocky artifacts while strictly preventing over-smoothing.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We present the unified implementation in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ B.2 Implementation of interpolation operators ‣ Appendix B Implementation details ‣ Just-in-Time: Training-Free Spatial Acceleration for Diffusion Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Unified Interpolation Operator (<math id="alg2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>)</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algx1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="algx1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span>Number of active tokens <math id="algx1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, total tokens <math id="algx1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, token dimension <math id="algx1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, active features <math id="algx1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{act}}\in\{\bm{u}_{\mathbf{act}},\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{\mathbf{act}}\}\in\mathbb{R}^{md}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐚𝐜𝐭</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>𝐚𝐜𝐭</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐚𝐜𝐭</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{act}}\in\{\bm{u}_{\mathbf{act}},\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{\mathbf{act}}\}\in\mathbb{R}^{md}</annotation></semantics></math>, active indices <math id="algx1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{\mathbf{act}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>𝐚𝐜𝐭</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{\mathbf{act}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="algx1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> Interpolated full tensor <math id="algx1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{full}}\in\{\bm{u}_{\mathbf{full}},\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{\mathbf{full}}\}\in\mathbb{R}^{Nd}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐟𝐮𝐥𝐥</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>𝐟𝐮𝐥𝐥</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐟𝐮𝐥𝐥</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{full}}\in\{\bm{u}_{\mathbf{full}},\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{\mathbf{full}}\}\in\mathbb{R}^{Nd}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="algx1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Nearest-Neighbor Interpolation</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
             Generate full coordinate grid <math id="algx1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}_{\mathbf{full}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>𝐟𝐮𝐥𝐥</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}_{\mathbf{full}}</annotation></semantics></math> and active coordinates <math id="algx1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}_{\mathbf{act}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>𝐚𝐜𝐭</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}_{\mathbf{act}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="algx1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each token <math id="algx1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="algx1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="algx1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{*}=\arg\min_{j\in\mathcal{A}_{\mathbf{act}}}\|\mathbf{C}_{\mathbf{full}}[i]-\mathbf{C}_{\mathbf{act}}[j]\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>𝐚𝐜𝐭</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>𝐟𝐮𝐥𝐥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>𝐚𝐜𝐭</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{*}=\arg\min_{j\in\mathcal{A}_{\mathbf{act}}}\|\mathbf{C}_{\mathbf{full}}[i]-\mathbf{C}_{\mathbf{act}}[j]\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="algx1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{NN}}[i]\leftarrow\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{act}}[j^{*}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐍𝐍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐚𝐜𝐭</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{NN}}[i]\leftarrow\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{act}}[j^{*}]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="algx1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="algx1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Controlled Gaussian Blur</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
             Calculate token density <math id="algx1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=m/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=m/N</annotation></semantics></math> and approximate anchor gap <math id="algx1.l10.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L\approx\rho^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≈</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\approx\rho^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
             Set blur scale <math id="algx1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.4L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.4L</annotation></semantics></math> and kernel size <math id="algx1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\approx 3\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\approx 3\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> {Ensure <math id="algx1.l11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;L</annotation></semantics></math> for adequate spatial coverage}

</div>
<div id="algx1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="algx1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{blur}}\leftarrow\text{GaussianBlur}(\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{NN}},\text{kernel}=k,\sigma=\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐛𝐥𝐮𝐫</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>GaussianBlur</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐍𝐍</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>kernel</mtext><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{blur}}\leftarrow\text{GaussianBlur}(\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{NN}},\text{kernel}=k,\sigma=\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="algx1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: Masked Composition</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
             Initialize binary mask <math id="algx1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}\leftarrow\mathbf{0}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}\leftarrow\mathbf{0}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="algx1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}[\mathcal{A}_{\mathbf{act}}]\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>𝐚𝐜𝐭</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}[\mathcal{A}_{\mathbf{act}}]\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> {Identify anchor positions}

</div>
<div id="algx1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="algx1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{full}}\leftarrow\mathbf{M}\odot\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{NN}}+(\mathbf{1}-\mathbf{M})\odot\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{blur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐟𝐮𝐥𝐥</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐍𝐍</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐛𝐥𝐮𝐫</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{full}}\leftarrow\mathbf{M}\odot\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{NN}}+(\mathbf{1}-\mathbf{M})\odot\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{blur}}</annotation></semantics></math> {Preserve exact anchor values}

</div>
<div id="algx1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="algx1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="algx1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{full}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐟𝐮𝐥𝐥</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{full}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Detailed experimental configurations</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in <a href="#A2.T4" title="In B.3 Detailed experimental configurations ‣ Appendix B Implementation details ‣ Just-in-Time: Training-Free Spatial Acceleration for Diffusion Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we provide the detailed hyperparameter settings for our JiT framework under the <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="7\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7\times</annotation></semantics></math> acceleration settings reported in the main paper. The configuration includes the total NFEs, the stage definition, and the specific token sparsity ratios used at each stage.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">It is important to note that these configurations are not the product of an exhaustive, brute-force search. Instead, they are derived from a principled and lightweight hyperparameter recipe. Specifically, we first determine an initial token sparsity threshold that strictly ensures semantic stability at the generation starting point. To achieve the target acceleration ratios (e.g., <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="7\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7\times</annotation></semantics></math>), we then strategically allocate the solver steps, assigning fewer steps to the highly sparse early stages to maximize inference speed, and dedicating more steps to the denser late stages to preserve fine-grained generation quality.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T4" class="ltx_table">
